        "The following process turns the source's lessons into a cautious learning workflow. It is not a recommendation to purchase any specific asset.\nStep 1: Establish financial readiness\nBefore investing, understand your basic financial position.\n- Know your regular income and expenses.\n- Avoid investing money needed for immediate obligations.\n- Consider whether you have an emergency reserve appropriate to your circumstances.\n- Understand expensive debt and its interest cost.\n- Decide how much money you can afford to expose to market risk.\nA small amount such as $100 can be a useful learning amount, but only if losing it would not affect essential needs.\nStep 2: Set a goal and time horizon\nWrite down:\n- What the investment is for.\n- When you may need the money.\n- Whether you need income or long-term growth.\n- How much volatility you can tolerate.\n- What would cause you to sell.\nAvoid selecting an asset before you know what job it is meant to perform.\nStep 3: Learn the investment type\nUse the relevant chapter in this playbook to understand the asset.",
