    "Conclusion: Start by Understanding What You Own\nThe source's comparison of five investment types shows that there is no single asset that wins every category.\n- Individual stocks offer direct company ownership but require research and expose investors to company-specific risk.\n- REITs provide property exposure and potential distributions without buying a building directly.\n- Cryptocurrency offers high volatility and speculative upside alongside serious security and loss risks.\n- Gold can act as a store-of-value exposure but does not produce income.\n- Index funds provide a relatively simple route to diversified market exposure, although they remain exposed to market declines.\nThe source's personal preference is to place the majority of its portfolio in index funds while holding smaller allocations across other investment types. That is the presenter's own approach, not a universal allocation to copy.",
